# 1. Operator Fusion: We combine the bias addition (from the Linear layer) and the two subsequent 
#    Mish activations into a single kernel. This dramatically reduces GPU memory bandwidth usage 
#    by avoiding writing/reading intermediate tensors (output of add, output of first mish) to/from global memory.
# 2. In-register computation: The intermediate values stay in registers.

